From: genshanxinli <127909456+genshanxinli@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:05:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fullconenat-nft: drop removed validate data parameter on Linux 6.6.113+/6.12+

Linux 6.12 (backported to 6.6.113) removed the unused third parameter
(const struct nft_data **data) from struct nft_expr_ops.validate(). Guard the
nft_fullcone_validate() signature with LINUX_VERSION_CODE so the module builds
against current kernels.

Origin: backport, archive/xr1710g-v1
Signed-off-by: genshanxinli <127909456+genshanxinli@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/src/nft_ext_fullcone.c b/src/nft_ext_fullcone.c
index 96d1feb..def862e 100644
--- a/src/nft_ext_fullcone.c
+++ b/src/nft_ext_fullcone.c
@@ -121,7 +121,12 @@ static int exp_event_cb(unsigned int events, const struct nf_exp_event *item)
 }
 #endif
 
+#if ((LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(6, 6, 113)) && (LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(6, 7, 0))) || \
+	(LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(6, 12, 0))
+static int nft_fullcone_validate(const struct nft_ctx *ctx, const struct nft_expr *expr)
+#else
 static int nft_fullcone_validate(const struct nft_ctx *ctx, const struct nft_expr *expr, const struct nft_data **data)
+#endif
 {
 	int err;
 
